WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:05.606
Why is an endless supply of health information actually making America sicker and poorer?

2
00:00:06.026 --> 00:00:11.366
Because our public health agencies were built for unified press briefings, not algorithmic feeds.

3
00:00:11.914 --> 00:00:16.166
Let's track a single piece of preventative guidance as it drops into a modern timeline.

4
00:00:16.842 --> 00:00:21.542
Instantly competes with confident wellness influencers and aggressive pharmaceutical ads.

5
00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:26.246
Behavioral science shows that when options multiply and credibility clashes,

6
00:00:26.506 --> 00:00:28.550
decision-making simply paralyzes.

7
00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:32.358
The public's willingness to follow evidence-based recommendations drops.

8
00:00:32.842 --> 00:00:34.246
It's a structural mismatch.

9
00:00:34.794 --> 00:00:38.534
Health institutions are trapped in slow, risk-averse review processes.

10
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.430
Unregulated voices are algorithmically rewarded for speed and emotional certainty.

11
00:00:44.106 --> 00:00:48.102
This broken communication creates a massive, preventable financial burden.

12
00:00:48.618 --> 00:00:53.190
When public confidence collapses, the downstream cost of treating the resulting emergencies

13
00:00:53.418 --> 00:00:57.030
exponentially dwarfs the cost of proactive, coherent communication.

14
00:00:57.738 --> 00:01:00.006
Health communication isn't just a medical issue.

15
00:01:00.394 --> 00:01:02.342
It is vital economic infrastructure.

16
00:01:02.698 --> 00:01:05.638
And investing in clarity is direct economic protection.

17
00:01:06.154 --> 00:01:08.614
Human in purpose. Systemic in method.

18
00:01:09.098 --> 00:01:10.214
Protective in outcome.
